      "description": "gov.uk publishes no MX records. Its published SPF record is 'v=spf1 -all'. Its SPF record authorises no senders at all, and its DMARC policy is p=reject, which together say this domain neither sends nor receives mail - so the absence of MX records looks deliberate rather than broken.",
      "impact": "A sending server has to wait for the lookup to fail and then fall back to the A record before giving up, which delays the bounce and can leave mail queued for days.",
      "remediation": "Publish the null MX record 'MX 0 .' (RFC 7505). It tells senders immediately and unambiguously that this domain accepts no mail, instead of leaving them to infer it.",
      "references": [
        "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7505"
      ],
